{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1181474-imbued-weapons-with-damage-spell-effects","id":1181474,"title":"Imbued Weapons with Damage Spell Effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-01T13:00:14-08:00","id":1181474,"title":"Imbued Weapons with Damage Spell Effects","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I know there was a thread created roughly 2 years ago and to prevent resurrecting an old thread, I decided to create a new thread. Hopefully this is ok, and it seems no clear answer was derived from the original thread anyway so hopefully more insight has been gained and handling this type of question is more refined since 2016.<br /> <br /> There is a player that wants to imbue a sword with &quot;Telekinetic Strike&quot; when it is swung at an opponent. So, how should this work mechanically, my questions are follows:<br /> Should the opponent suffer damage from the attack regardless of being hit? Should the spell be considered a thrown spell? Should the weapon damage override the damage spell if greater? The spell damage itself is Bashing while the sword damage is Lethal, so I am really torn on how this should work.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:23:35-08:00","id":1181480,"title":"","content":"I will admit that I have taken almost no time to consider the mechanics of imbued items. However, my instinct would be that since a sword requires someone to hit something in order to normally do anything to it, I would say that symbolically it wouldn't make sense for the trigger to release the spell to be anything other than actually striking the target. As to damage, I would personally say it's additive: that is to say I would rule it that the damage would stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:24:28-08:00","id":1181481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1181474-imbued-weapons-with-damage-spell-effects#post1181474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I know there was a thread created roughly 2 years ago and to prevent resurrecting an old thread, I decided to create a new thread. Hopefully this is ok, and it seems no clear answer was derived from the original thread anyway so hopefully more insight has been gained and handling this type of question is more refined since 2016.<br /> <br /> There is a player that wants to imbue a sword with &quot;Telekinetic Strike&quot; when it is swung at an opponent. So, how should this work mechanically, my questions are follows:<br /> Should the opponent suffer damage from the attack regardless of being hit? Should the spell be considered a thrown spell? Should the weapon damage override the damage spell if greater? The spell damage itself is Bashing while the sword damage is Lethal, so I am really torn on how this should work.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, what is the trigger? When swung? When the blade connects (which is odd for that spell)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:25:33-08:00","id":1181482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1181474-imbued-weapons-with-damage-spell-effects?p=1181481#post1181481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, what is the trigger? When swung? When the blade connects (which is odd for that spell)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey Vent0, the trigger is when swung.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T13:26:13-08:00","id":1181483,"title":"","content":"I think there's a couple ways to look at it:<br /> <br /> 1) It's a sword that happens to be able to cast Telekinetic Strike. Meaning, with one action, you can either use it as a sword, or as an Imbued Item to cast the spell. The two function independently. If you want the spell to be ranged, this is how I would do it (gnosis+athletics/firearms to hit as a thrown spell).<br /> or<br /> 2) It you want it to be &quot;on hit&quot;, set the trigger for the imbued spell to be &quot;I hit something with the blade&quot;. In this case, you'd want the spell's range to be touch. You would roll to hit with the sword normally (Strength+Melee) and on any hit the spell would go off on whatever the blade is touching (so I would apply armor against the spell's damage). The damage from getting hit by a sword is independent of the spell, so they would both apply as normal. Keep in mind that the spell is having no effect on the blade itself, so it won't alter the sword's properties in anyway (except to make it a container and trigger for the spell), hence the sword still does lethal while the spell does bashing. The target get's hit by a sword, and then get's punched by magic.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what you seem to be envisioning would be better represented by a permeant &quot;Telekinetic <i>Blow</i>&quot; spell with the Reach option that allows it to affect weapons. The spell's main purpose is to &quot;upgrade&quot; the damage of an attack: the weapon increase its weapon modifier by Potency (up to 5), and you can use Reach to add stun or knock-back. Even better, the spell is only 2-dots, so it's cheaper/easier to cast than Telekinetic Strike.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps. (I've given a lot of thought to how enchanted weapons work, since one of my players keeps trying to make a sword that eats souls).<br /> <br /> Edit in response to ninja-ing: If you're imagining the sword firing magical projectiles &quot;on swing&quot;, see what I said above, but also consider that if you were to try and hit with the blade at the same time, it'd be a bit like trying to hit a baseball and clobber someone with the bat at the same time. Possible, but a kinda tricky to line up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 02-01-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T15:00:58-08:00","id":1181500,"title":"","content":"Hey Scriptorian,<br /> <br /> Thanks, this definitely helped me conceptualize what I needed to do. Appreciate the assistance. I will see if the trigger can be changed to &quot;on hit&quot; since it is must simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:25:52-08:00","id":1181530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1181474-imbued-weapons-with-damage-spell-effects?p=1181500#post1181500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Scriptorian,<br /> <br /> Thanks, this definitely helped me conceptualize what I needed to do. Appreciate the assistance. I will see if the trigger can be changed to &quot;on hit&quot; since it is must simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, but then you lose the ranged capability and faux-Master Sword-ness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T06:09:50-08:00","id":1182240,"title":"","content":"Trigger: While bearing no Wounds and after being swung and briefly pointing, <i>Telekinetic Strike</i> is activated as a thrown spell.<br /> Secondary Trigger: After a successful meditation roll, release for an AoE <i>Telekinetic Strike</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}